WEBVTT

00:02.740 --> 00:06.980
I never would've expected to run into 
another target in a place like this.

00:06.980 --> 00:09.050
Zenos! Zenos?!

00:10.560 --> 00:13.750
While I'm working on a 
different, bigger case,

00:13.750 --> 00:17.200
I've also been investigating a string 
of children who've been kidnapped.

00:17.200 --> 00:18.550
Zenos didn't...

00:19.200 --> 00:21.140
You're an elf child.

00:21.140 --> 00:23.080
But he is a human.

00:23.080 --> 00:25.650
That means you're not family.

00:25.650 --> 00:27.450
So I've finally found him.

00:27.450 --> 00:31.420
Clever trick, setting up shop in a desolate 
place like this where no one is around.

00:31.420 --> 00:32.740
Y-You've got it all wrong!

00:32.740 --> 00:34.510
Zenos took me in!

00:34.510 --> 00:37.600
Humanoid trafficking is illegal unless 
conducted through proper channels.

00:37.600 --> 00:39.100
That's not what I meant!

00:39.100 --> 00:42.020
Zenos saved me!

00:42.020 --> 00:44.140
What? Did I jump to conclusions?

00:44.430 --> 00:46.190
You really did!

00:46.400 --> 00:50.780
Forgive me, then. That was a 
round for apprehending suspects.

00:50.780 --> 00:53.490
It shouldn't be lethal, but he 
won't be waking up for a while.

00:53.490 --> 00:55.810
I'm a perfectionist with my work,

00:55.810 --> 00:58.660
but my short temper is my only real fault.

00:58.660 --> 01:03.260
I thought you said your only real fault 
was having a bad sense of direction?

01:03.870 --> 01:05.460
What in the world?

02:38.480 --> 02:40.010
What in the world?

02:41.240 --> 02:42.790
My sincere apologies.

02:42.790 --> 02:44.500
I seem to have jumped to conclusions.

02:45.020 --> 02:47.430
I'm relieved you're all right, but... how?

02:47.680 --> 02:49.660
I just used some defensive magic.

02:49.660 --> 02:50.870
You must be kidding.

02:50.870 --> 02:54.320
Defensive magic isn't capable 
of stopping my magic guns.

02:54.320 --> 02:57.400
I mean, as far as I know, 
it was ordinary defensive magic.

02:57.400 --> 02:59.180
Are you being serious?

03:04.330 --> 03:06.700
You're definitely unhurt.

03:06.700 --> 03:08.170
How is this possible?

03:08.170 --> 03:10.750
So many things today have 
been utterly inexplicable...

03:10.750 --> 03:15.840
Getting shot by someone I've never met 
before falls in that category for me.

03:16.100 --> 03:18.630
Are you some sort of 
renowned grand sorcerer?

03:18.630 --> 03:22.090
Devoting your heart and soul to 
defensive magic from an early age,

03:22.090 --> 03:24.970
mastering your field of study, 
earning you the name...

03:24.970 --> 03:26.760
"He Who Worked Hard at Defensive Magic."

03:26.760 --> 03:29.620
First, wrong. Second, your 
naming sense is terrible.

03:29.620 --> 03:33.030
My lack of naming talent is my only fault.

03:33.030 --> 03:34.400
That's another one, isn't it?

03:34.400 --> 03:37.460
That's the only explanation 
that makes sense, though.

03:37.460 --> 03:39.190
Though others may not be able to tell,

03:39.190 --> 03:43.030
there's no deceiving the eyes of Vice Commander 
Krishna of the Royal Order of Knights.

03:44.400 --> 03:47.370
Vice Commander... of the 
Royal Order of Knights?

03:47.370 --> 03:50.000
Indeed. I believe you are Mr. Zenos, yes?

03:50.000 --> 03:53.040
I'd appreciate it if you would 
cooperate with my investigation.

03:55.960 --> 03:59.840
<i>I put up a signal for everyone to stay 
away, given the nature of the situation,</i>

03:59.840 --> 04:02.170
<i>so I don't think they'll 
waltz in here, but...</i>

04:02.170 --> 04:06.140
I've actually come to the 
slums on a secret mission.

04:06.500 --> 04:09.220
Is that the kind of thing 
you should be sharing?

04:09.220 --> 04:13.480
My secret mission is to locate a certain 
individual and take them into custody.

04:13.480 --> 04:15.310
You're just laying it all out there, huh?

04:15.310 --> 04:19.440
I doubt I can gain your cooperation 
without sharing some degree of specifics.

04:19.440 --> 04:22.070
I never said anything about cooperating...

04:22.070 --> 04:25.070
It's the duty of every citizen to 
cooperate with the Order of Knights!

04:25.360 --> 04:28.160
<i>I guess she doesn't listen, either.</i>

04:28.160 --> 04:30.410
So, who are you looking for?

04:31.800 --> 04:32.910
The mediator.

04:33.440 --> 04:36.710
Whoever ended the feud between 
the factions in the slums.

04:37.360 --> 04:38.450
What's wrong?

04:38.450 --> 04:40.710
Oh, uh, it's nothing.

04:41.690 --> 04:43.050
<i>You little...</i>

04:43.050 --> 04:44.780
As a defender of order,

04:44.780 --> 04:48.760
I can't ignore the appearance of 
someone who wields that kind of power.

04:49.180 --> 04:53.300
But I was unable to get anything out of the 
demihumans, even after shaking them down.

04:53.300 --> 04:56.310
Whoever this person is, they're 
well-versed in how to control people...

04:56.310 --> 04:59.190
Such deeds no doubt mark him 
as a servant of the devil!

04:59.550 --> 05:01.610
<i>A servant of the devil?</i>

05:01.610 --> 05:05.300
The guy might just want 
to avoid the spotlight.

05:05.300 --> 05:07.410
Y'know, maybe he doesn't want attention?

05:07.410 --> 05:10.450
Maybe leaving him be and not looking 
too hard for him would be best.

05:10.450 --> 05:12.660
Do you know the mediator?!

05:12.920 --> 05:14.990
Nah, that's just my instinct talking!

05:18.280 --> 05:21.450
Someone with the power to unify 
the rival factions in the slums

05:21.450 --> 05:25.420
could pose a threat to the 
nation itself in time.

05:26.430 --> 05:31.150
I don't think they're thinking 
of anything that big.

05:31.150 --> 05:34.120
They might be kind of a stickler 
about money, but deep down,

05:34.120 --> 05:38.980
I bet they just don't like 
seeing people get hurt.

05:39.580 --> 05:40.460
Lily...

05:41.320 --> 05:43.670
Do you know who the mediator is, elf girl?

05:43.670 --> 05:47.530
N-N-Nope! I don't know a thing!

05:49.900 --> 05:51.120
No matter.

05:51.120 --> 05:54.580
I anticipated having trouble 
even finding his trail.

05:54.580 --> 05:58.250
Maybe it's time for you to go.
I'll show you the way back to town.

05:58.250 --> 06:00.290
You seem to want me gone.

06:00.290 --> 06:03.800
W-Well, it's just... you've got 
an important mission, right?

06:04.180 --> 06:05.800
You have a point.

06:06.620 --> 06:08.930
I should be on my way.

06:13.140 --> 06:15.430
Why is there a bed down here?

06:16.510 --> 06:20.810
It's, uh, an extra bed. I brought 
it out here to throw it away.

06:20.810 --> 06:25.280
In that case... I'd appreciate 
you letting me use it.

06:26.320 --> 06:28.800
I've actually had trouble 
finding a base of operations.

06:28.800 --> 06:31.550
Here, I'll be close to the slums 
without attracting attention.

06:31.550 --> 06:32.990
It's ideal for my investigation.

06:33.220 --> 06:35.620
Of course, I will pay for my stay.

06:35.620 --> 06:40.460
I need to find the root of this new evil, 
the mediator, and capture him myself.

06:40.880 --> 06:43.710
From servant of the devil 
to the root of evil...

06:43.960 --> 06:46.770
"And so, as had become 
so common at this point,

06:46.770 --> 06:49.900
the clinic welcomed a new, dangerous woman."

06:52.180 --> 06:53.710
It's nothing fancy, but...

06:53.710 --> 06:55.580
I appreciate it.

06:56.700 --> 06:57.520
Hot!

06:58.340 --> 06:59.520
Pardon me.

06:59.520 --> 07:03.040
My sensitivity to hot foods 
and drinks is my one fault.

07:03.040 --> 07:04.630
You have a lot of faults, huh?

07:04.630 --> 07:07.860
What are you saying?
I only have one fault.

07:08.540 --> 07:09.650
I see...

07:11.910 --> 07:13.280
What's wrong, Lily?

07:13.280 --> 07:15.030
Zenos, lap.

07:20.240 --> 07:22.120
Zenos, my usual.

07:22.120 --> 07:23.630
Your usual?

07:23.870 --> 07:26.340
My! Usual!

07:35.310 --> 07:36.590
It's jealousy.

07:36.590 --> 07:37.890
Don't scare me like that!

07:37.890 --> 07:39.080
Something wrong?

07:39.080 --> 07:41.110
Uh, n-no, nothing.

07:41.110 --> 07:42.130
I see.

07:42.980 --> 07:46.120
I've gone invisible and 
am whispering in your ear.

07:46.120 --> 07:48.530
Well, I wish you wouldn't.
It's bad for my heart.

07:48.530 --> 07:51.110
So, why would Lily be jealous?

07:51.110 --> 07:54.780
She's trying to demonstrate her advantage 
to this random new challenger!

07:54.780 --> 07:59.160
"I'm much closer to Zenos than you are!"

07:59.160 --> 08:02.080
She has no intention of accepting 
this oddly haughty woman

08:02.080 --> 08:04.920
who blasted you at random with a magic gun!

08:04.920 --> 08:09.340
To say nothing of the contrast between 
the dour attitude and the sensitive tongue!

08:09.340 --> 08:12.130
But what can she do? What's her next move?

08:12.130 --> 08:14.750
The bell is rung for this 
battle between women!

08:14.750 --> 08:16.180
Pipe down.

08:16.830 --> 08:19.300
Zenos, your tea's still hot,

08:19.300 --> 08:21.140
so I'll blow on it for you.

08:21.520 --> 08:23.910
Zenos, your hair's sticking up.

08:23.910 --> 08:25.650
I'll fix it for you.

08:26.020 --> 08:27.730
Zenos, here's an apple.

08:27.730 --> 08:29.700
I'll feed it to you!

08:34.780 --> 08:38.910
I'll just have to use the secret 
weapon Carmilla taught me!

08:40.410 --> 08:43.660
Zenos... T-Tonight,

08:43.660 --> 08:46.630
I'm not going to let you sleep...

08:49.800 --> 08:51.420
She's sound asleep.

08:51.420 --> 08:52.460
Yeah.

08:54.470 --> 08:56.140
I win...

08:59.390 --> 09:00.820
What is it?

09:00.820 --> 09:04.890
You said that elf girl had 
been caught by slave traders.

09:04.890 --> 09:06.560
Do you know who they are?

09:06.560 --> 09:08.360
No, I don't.

09:08.360 --> 09:09.890
I see.

09:09.890 --> 09:13.650
It seems like there's a hotbed for 
child trafficking around here.

09:13.650 --> 09:16.200
And that's why you shot me?

09:16.200 --> 09:18.360
I'm sorry about that.

09:18.360 --> 09:21.200
Having a short temper is my one fault.

09:21.200 --> 09:24.710
It really does sound like you have a 
lot of faults. Not that it matters.

09:25.050 --> 09:29.790
I am meant to be a perfect member of the 
royal guard, as well as a hero to the people.

09:29.790 --> 09:33.340
I am allowed to have, at most, one fault.

09:33.870 --> 09:35.130
I have a question.

09:35.680 --> 09:38.610
You're a master mage who has 
perfected defense magic, yes?

09:38.610 --> 09:39.800
Not at all.

09:40.160 --> 09:44.660
If someone was able to master healing 
magic the way you've mastered defense,

09:44.660 --> 09:48.240
would they be able to 
fully regenerate an arm?

09:48.240 --> 09:49.810
Uh, do other healers—

09:48.870 --> 09:50.890
No, it can't be possible.

09:50.890 --> 09:55.280
Not for anyone other than a Saint or a 
handful of the highest-level top-secret healers.

09:55.280 --> 09:56.990
What's it matter?

09:56.990 --> 09:59.600
In a fight with Zophia the Tornado,

09:59.600 --> 10:01.660
I did a fair amount of damage to her arm.

10:02.080 --> 10:04.170
Yet when I saw her and 
her minion in the slums,

10:04.170 --> 10:06.710
their arms were completely back to normal.

10:06.710 --> 10:10.810
If there's someone who can 
heal those kinds of wounds,

10:10.810 --> 10:13.660
their words might have real gravity.

10:14.960 --> 10:18.560
Well, I can begin my investigation 
in earnest tomorrow.

10:18.560 --> 10:23.760
I will arrest this agitator of the slums, 
and the original evil, the mediator.

10:24.190 --> 10:28.150
The original evil? 
These allegations keep leveling up...

10:28.150 --> 10:31.650
What makes you feel so 
threatened by the slums, anyway?

10:31.940 --> 10:34.110
It's not much of a story.

10:34.400 --> 10:37.690
My mother was killed by 
someone who lived there.

10:39.360 --> 10:41.680
She was a profoundly kind woman.

10:42.220 --> 10:48.500
She visited the slums 
daily to feed the hungry.

10:48.910 --> 10:52.420
And one day, she returned as a corpse.

10:52.420 --> 10:56.130
I was told it was a crime done 
to steal her wedding ring.

10:56.440 --> 11:00.220
She had saved so many from hunger,

11:00.220 --> 11:02.300
but no one was there to save her.

11:03.440 --> 11:05.950
That is why I decided that I would become

11:05.950 --> 11:09.150
an invincible hero 
capable of delivering justice

11:09.150 --> 11:11.040
to the criminals of the slums,

11:11.040 --> 11:13.690
so what happened to her would 
never happen to anyone else.

11:13.690 --> 11:15.950
I achieved distinction early on

11:15.950 --> 11:19.400
and became the youngest vice commander 
in the history of the Royal Knights.

11:19.400 --> 11:25.700
My unbendable will regarding my duties 
eventually earned me the nickname "Iron Rose."

11:26.010 --> 11:30.770
Some people seem to use it to suggest 
I'm unreasonable and don't listen,

11:30.770 --> 11:34.790
but I know the other thing 
attributed to that name.

11:35.820 --> 11:39.250
My face is like an iron 
mask, wouldn't you say?

11:40.310 --> 11:44.330
Ever since that day, 
I've had trouble smiling.

11:50.020 --> 11:52.070
I'll be back tonight, then.

11:54.000 --> 11:56.400
Don't pay it any mind, Zenos.

11:56.400 --> 11:58.810
Her story isn't that unusual.

11:58.810 --> 12:00.500
When you live 300 years,

12:00.500 --> 12:04.070
you witness all the ways a 
person's life can turn out.

12:04.070 --> 12:06.780
You came down just to say that?

12:07.090 --> 12:08.910
I appreciate it, Carmilla.

12:10.620 --> 12:13.330
I'm just not fond of all 
this sentimental morbidity!

12:13.630 --> 12:15.120
What about the flag?

12:15.120 --> 12:17.670
Well, I guess I'll take it down for now.

12:19.210 --> 12:20.960
Try to be more careful, okay?

12:21.590 --> 12:23.280
Sorry, Doc.

12:23.280 --> 12:26.850
By the way, one of my boys mentioned 
that the knight I told you about—

12:26.850 --> 12:29.560
Mr. Zenos, I'm sorry, but I got lost and...

12:31.850 --> 12:35.310
Iron Rose! What are you doing here?!

12:31.850 --> 12:35.310
Zophia the Tornado, what are you doing here?!

12:35.310 --> 12:37.270
I-It's not what you think!

12:37.270 --> 12:39.520
You sound like a husband caught cheating.

12:39.860 --> 12:43.150
This lady says... sh-she got lost, too!

12:43.150 --> 12:45.270
She got lost and ended up here?

12:45.270 --> 12:46.940
She must be quite directionless.

12:46.940 --> 12:48.030
Yeah, <i>you</i> are.

12:48.030 --> 12:49.920
You heard the girl. There a problem?

12:49.920 --> 12:53.120
I just got lost and was 
asking for directions.

12:53.120 --> 12:56.040
What happened to your 
arm, Zophia the Tornado?

12:57.290 --> 13:01.030
I believe that it was the 
mediator who healed it.

13:01.030 --> 13:03.220
The person gathering up 
the criminal elements

13:03.220 --> 13:06.090
of the slums to threaten 
its innocent residents.

13:07.120 --> 13:10.220
Threaten the residents of the slums?

13:10.220 --> 13:13.700
I'm a two-bit rogue, so I probably 
don't have a leg to stand on here,

13:13.700 --> 13:16.650
but you can find crooks 
on all rungs of society.

13:16.650 --> 13:17.980
What are you getting at?

13:17.980 --> 13:22.560
I hear the Royal Knights are investigating 
the child trafficking ring,

13:22.560 --> 13:25.150
but did you know that their 
boss was an aristocrat?

13:25.430 --> 13:28.320
The child trafficking ring 
is centered in the slums.

13:28.320 --> 13:31.910
That's just where the rank and file 
operate to throw off the scent.

13:31.910 --> 13:33.200
I find that hard to believe.

13:33.450 --> 13:34.610
I bet.

13:34.610 --> 13:37.000
It's not like you'd ever 
listen to us, anyway.

13:37.950 --> 13:39.580
Who do you claim it is, then?

13:39.880 --> 13:41.170
Calendor.

13:41.450 --> 13:43.180
Even more ridiculous.

13:43.180 --> 13:46.050
He's a philanthropist who's 
passionate about educating orphans.

13:46.050 --> 13:50.080
The way you only look at the surface
is what makes you easy to trick.

13:50.080 --> 13:52.010
Not the mediator, though.

13:52.400 --> 13:55.360
They never judged any of 
us because of our status

13:55.360 --> 13:56.940
or the way we look.

13:56.940 --> 13:59.600
All they ever did was save 
the people who needed it.

14:00.000 --> 14:03.020
Hell, as much as I hate to admit it,

14:03.020 --> 14:05.520
he'd probably save your life, 
too, if you were hurt.

14:05.520 --> 14:07.240
Just not for free.

14:07.630 --> 14:11.390
Nothing like you, who's convinced 
that all evil comes from the slums.

14:11.390 --> 14:14.540
Your idea of justice is a joke.

14:14.540 --> 14:15.910
How dare you?

14:18.290 --> 14:20.530
Mr. Zenos, stand aside.

14:20.530 --> 14:22.390
Sorry, but that's not happening.

14:22.390 --> 14:24.480
Zophia is one of my patients.

14:24.480 --> 14:25.760
Patients?

14:26.080 --> 14:29.000
I'm sorry for not telling 
you sooner, Krishna.

14:29.000 --> 14:30.550
I'm the mediator.

14:30.840 --> 14:33.140
You're the mediator?

14:33.420 --> 14:34.100
Yeah.

14:34.100 --> 14:37.930
Inconceivable. The mediator 
is a master of healing magic.

14:38.190 --> 14:41.160
But your specialty is defensive magic.

14:41.160 --> 14:44.190
It'd be impossible to wield two 
schools of magic at such a high level.

14:44.570 --> 14:47.760
I'm not exactly a master, and both 
defense and healing are about

14:47.760 --> 14:51.030
amplifying the body's natural functions, 
so they're basically the same.

14:51.490 --> 14:54.990
I've never heard that kind of 
logic in any of my magic lessons.

14:55.690 --> 15:01.710
But one thing that's clear is that you've 
sided with the demihumans and the mediator.

15:02.150 --> 15:04.720
I'll find a different place to work from.

15:04.720 --> 15:06.050
Krishna...

15:06.050 --> 15:08.920
The people need a perfect hero.

15:09.540 --> 15:11.590
And I am no joke.

15:16.480 --> 15:20.480
She's headed in the opposite 
direction from the slums...

15:20.480 --> 15:22.570
She could get lost on a one-way street.

15:24.190 --> 15:26.300
Wait, is she...

15:29.660 --> 15:35.160
A sudden visit from the Vice Commander of the 
Royal Order of the Knights is quite a surprise.

15:35.430 --> 15:40.660
Lord Calendor, are you aware that there have 
been thieves operating in this area as of late?

15:40.660 --> 15:44.380
I did hear something about 
a band of lizardman thieves.

15:44.380 --> 15:48.960
Yes. It is our intention to 
increase local security.

15:48.960 --> 15:53.760
We'd appreciate it if you and your 
fellow nobles would be more careful.

15:55.020 --> 15:59.930
As part of that, I'd like to do a 
security assessment of your manor.

15:59.930 --> 16:02.300
A splendid idea!

16:02.300 --> 16:06.820
That said, if you had told me beforehand, 
I could've been better prepared.

16:06.820 --> 16:09.730
Our intent is to get the best 
grasp of the usual level of security.

16:09.730 --> 16:12.860
I beg your pardon, but a surprise 
inspection would be more effective.

16:14.750 --> 16:16.030
Very well, then!

16:17.660 --> 16:21.660
<i>Zophia the Tornado claimed Lord 
Calendor was the ringleader,</i>

16:21.660 --> 16:24.080
<i>but I'm wasting my time here.</i>

16:24.080 --> 16:26.960
What do you say, Lady Krishna?

16:26.960 --> 16:28.880
Your security is quite thorough.

16:28.880 --> 16:31.510
If I had to point anything 
out, it'd be the distri—

16:32.180 --> 16:33.840
Is something wrong?

16:34.570 --> 16:36.220
No, not a thing.

16:36.510 --> 16:39.460
Would it be all right if I used your 
washroom before I take my leave?

16:39.460 --> 16:41.100
By all means.

16:41.820 --> 16:45.600
<i>Lord Calendor sits somewhere in the 
upper-mid echelon of the aristocracy.</i>

16:45.600 --> 16:47.560
<i>GIven that, it's odd how much security he has.</i>

16:47.560 --> 16:49.480
<i>And then there's the distribution of it.</i>

16:49.480 --> 16:52.530
<i>The rear entrance seems to have 
a lot more guards than the front.</i>

16:54.250 --> 16:55.510
<i>It couldn't be...</i>

17:08.760 --> 17:10.050
Oh, no.

17:14.180 --> 17:16.630
Who's there? S-Someone scary?

17:16.630 --> 17:20.600
It's all right. I'm not here to hurt you.

17:20.600 --> 17:22.220
Who are you?

17:22.550 --> 17:25.750
Me? I'm a hero, here to save you.

17:31.900 --> 17:36.910
The magic guns you royal knights 
use are quite powerful!

17:36.910 --> 17:40.120
This will be perfect for 
threatening the children, too.

17:42.120 --> 17:47.290
I can't say I appreciate a mere knight like 
you sniffing about the business of a noble.

17:47.290 --> 17:51.590
Your job is to stay quiet 
and keep the rabble in line!

17:53.120 --> 17:57.760
The flawless Iron Rose, 
reduced to a wounded heap!

17:57.760 --> 18:00.150
<i>I'm sorry, children.</i>

18:01.080 --> 18:02.320
<i>Mother...</i>

18:02.760 --> 18:06.700
<i>I... wasn't able to be a real hero.</i>

18:07.310 --> 18:09.690
Aw, damn, she's still alive?

18:09.690 --> 18:12.190
We should've taken a bit longer to get here.

18:12.620 --> 18:14.900
Zophia the Tornado?

18:15.150 --> 18:16.950
W-Why?

18:16.950 --> 18:18.720
This was a crazy move.

18:18.720 --> 18:22.410
You don't disappoint, and that's 
not meant as a compliment.

18:22.410 --> 18:24.640
I went out of my way for this house call.

18:24.640 --> 18:27.580
It's going to cost a lot, so brace yourself.

18:27.580 --> 18:29.060
Who are you people?!

18:29.060 --> 18:30.080
Don't worry about me.

18:30.080 --> 18:31.960
I'm just an unremarkable healer.

18:31.960 --> 18:34.220
And I just showed him the way.

18:34.220 --> 18:35.860
E-Enough comedy!

18:35.860 --> 18:37.880
You're a lizardman, right?

18:38.160 --> 18:42.940
No one will complain if I kill 
some thief from the slums.

18:42.940 --> 18:44.600
Now, stand down!

18:51.520 --> 18:52.690
Fool!

18:52.690 --> 18:54.260
That actually kinda hurt.

18:54.770 --> 18:56.570
What?!

18:56.900 --> 19:00.400
You... Wh-Why?! Why isn't it working?!

19:00.400 --> 19:03.370
Why?! Why?! Why?!

19:11.880 --> 19:15.750
What is this? What in the world are you?!

19:17.670 --> 19:21.360
A low-born dog like you dares to 
point that gun at an aristocrat?!

19:21.360 --> 19:24.850
I hear you shouldn't shoot at people 
unless you're prepared to be shot.

19:24.850 --> 19:29.480
W-Wait! I-I'll do whatever you 
want! Just lower the gun!

19:29.480 --> 19:32.710
Well, to be honest, we've just met,

19:32.710 --> 19:35.230
and it's not like I have some 
old grudge against you.

19:35.230 --> 19:38.650
The only thing I have against you is that 
you were blasting at me a second ago.

19:38.650 --> 19:41.220
F-Forgive me!

19:41.220 --> 19:44.910
And that's an apology from someone of 
my standing! Now, please, show mercy.

19:45.200 --> 19:46.200
Nope.

19:46.200 --> 19:48.560
Wh-Why?!

19:48.560 --> 19:52.960
I-I know! I just need to apologize 
to the woman, too, right?

19:53.880 --> 19:55.840
I was wrong.

19:55.840 --> 19:59.630
I got carried away when I fired 
on you. Please, forgive me.

20:01.200 --> 20:03.800
That was a pretty poor 
excuse for an apology,

20:03.800 --> 20:07.430
but I see someone else that you 
really ought to be apologizing to.

20:07.430 --> 20:10.310
A-And who would that be?!

20:10.310 --> 20:13.060
Since you can't seem to figure 
it out, you get punished.

20:13.360 --> 20:16.560
What did you think you were 
doing with my future patients?!

20:21.570 --> 20:24.160
Did you... kill him?

20:24.160 --> 20:26.660
The limiter was on, so he shouldn't be dead.

20:26.660 --> 20:29.950
It's not my duty to judge him anyway, right?

20:30.880 --> 20:34.210
It's... too late for me...

20:34.210 --> 20:36.750
Report what's happened... 
to the Royal Knights...

20:36.750 --> 20:39.200
Nah, that sounds like a lot of work.

20:39.200 --> 20:41.260
I'll let you take care of it.

20:41.630 --> 20:45.930
Your left arm, along with a chunk of 
your torso, and the organs to match.

20:46.290 --> 20:48.890
Such a defeated look after 
a little hit like this?

20:49.140 --> 20:51.000
So much for the Iron Rose.

20:52.150 --> 20:54.390
Don't be shocked when 
you get my invoice, okay?

20:54.810 --> 20:58.110
Mr. Zenos... Just who are you?

20:58.430 --> 21:00.400
Quiet. I'm trying to concentrate.

21:01.050 --> 21:02.560
You're a hero...

21:02.560 --> 21:04.580
Nothing that extravagant.

21:04.580 --> 21:07.410
I'm just an underground healer 
working out of a run-down clinic.

21:10.240 --> 21:11.580
Unbelievable.

21:11.960 --> 21:14.000
This kind of incredible healing...

21:14.000 --> 21:16.370
You really must be the mediator, Mr. Zenos.

21:16.370 --> 21:18.420
I literally told you that.

21:18.420 --> 21:21.100
I was no hero at all.

21:21.100 --> 21:25.060
I know now that a perfect 
hero is someone like you.

21:25.060 --> 21:28.300
There's no such thing as 
a perfect hero, anyway.

21:28.300 --> 21:32.540
People who fight for the sake of something 
are gonna get hurt, one way or another.

21:32.540 --> 21:34.890
That's why they need healers like me.

21:34.890 --> 21:36.810
Or so I was taught, anyway.

21:37.380 --> 21:40.570
I think, to them, you're the hero here.

21:40.980 --> 21:42.080
Them?

21:42.570 --> 21:47.240
Wh-What happened? 
Is the hero lady still there?

21:47.240 --> 21:49.200
You were the first one to take action.

21:49.200 --> 21:51.780
That makes you the hero in this case.

21:51.780 --> 21:56.110
I'm... I...

21:56.660 --> 22:01.960
K-Kids! It's all right! I'm still okay! 
I'll get you out of there soon!

22:02.750 --> 22:04.760
Thank you, hero!

22:05.330 --> 22:08.470
All this time, I thought my 
mother was a pitiable victim.

22:08.890 --> 22:12.600
But... her eyes were always shining.

22:12.600 --> 22:16.390
She would feed the children of the slums 
with food that she made herself.

22:16.720 --> 22:20.720
Yeah. Just like you're a hero to these kids,

22:20.720 --> 22:23.610
I bet she was someone's hero, too.

22:23.610 --> 22:30.200
My mother was... awkward, panicky, 
short-tempered, forgetful,

22:30.200 --> 22:32.550
and full of faults, really...

22:33.910 --> 22:41.080
But still... in spite of it all, 
I know for a fact that she was my hero.

22:48.200 --> 22:52.500
Doc, the royal knights are gonna 
catch on to the fuss any time now.

22:52.500 --> 22:55.260
Yeah. It's time for us to 
slink back into the shadows.

22:55.260 --> 22:56.520
Mr. Zenos!

23:00.770 --> 23:04.060
Mr. Zenos, why did you save me?

23:04.560 --> 23:06.070
Unpaid bills.

23:07.000 --> 23:10.410
You said you were gonna pay for 
using the clinic's bed, remember?

23:10.410 --> 23:13.240
If you got yourself killed,
I wouldn't be able to collect.

23:13.240 --> 23:16.790
I'm adding the fee for healing you to the 
cost. Make sure you pay it all back at once.

23:17.380 --> 23:18.940
The money I owed you...

23:28.050 --> 23:30.220
Looks like you can smile after all.

23:31.570 --> 23:36.350
I see. I'm smiling now, huh?

23:36.350 --> 23:38.890
Still looks pretty awkward, though.

23:38.890 --> 23:42.020
Hell, I think it makes 
you look even creepier.

23:42.020 --> 23:43.990
Wh-What do you want?

23:43.990 --> 23:46.240
It's been a long time since I've smiled.

23:46.240 --> 23:49.130
Not being good at it is my only...

23:49.720 --> 23:50.560
No...

23:51.110 --> 23:54.220
Just one of my many faults!

23:55.580 --> 24:00.040
A Place To Belong

23:57.690 --> 23:58.680
"A Place To Belong."
